Setting Purge ID pend flags if any items exist that CANNOT be purged yet - For Each Row confirm DATECANBEDELETED is current date or in past THEN delete attempt can take place
If single task/workpacket exists where CANDELETE date is in the future, then set PURGEAUDIT.DATADELETEPENDFLG = Y for the PURGEID
If single docid exists where CANDELETE date is in the future, then set PURGEAUDIT.DOCDELETEPENDFLG = Y for the PURGEID
SP will cycle through PURGETASK and PURGEWRKPKT and PURGEDOC for each PURGEID where PURGEAUDIT.ALLTASKDATAPURGEDFLG = N                                 
DELETING TSKID,PKTID,DOCID rows in Primary Tables and Secondary Tables (any table listed in PURGETABLECONFIG where LEVEL in PKTID or TSKID)                              
IF all Task Data has been purged update TASKPURGEFLG = Y for PURGEID in PURGETASK      
IF all PKTID data has been purged update WRKPKTPURGEDFLG = Y for PURGEID in PURGEWORKPKT
IF all DOC DATA has been purged update DOCDATAPURGEDFLG = Y for PURGEID in PURGEDOC
THEN IF all rows in PURGETASK,PURGEWORKPKT, and PURGEDOC for PURGEID have PURGEFLG = Y 
Update PURGEAUDIT.ALLTASKDATAPURGED = Y
PURGECASE Placeholder
For each row of data that is deleted populate DELETEDATE with current date for row
For documents, as part of this process, it should only update DOCDATADELETEDATE column with current date



